{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Mannix Squared JSFX\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A collection of JSFX effects for REAPER, distributed through ReaPack.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 ReaCrusher\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Stereo distortion, resonant low-pass filtering and compression for REAPER. An original scalable interface, seven knobs, linked stereo processing, and 20 factory presets plus Clear using REAPER's native preset menu.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The interface uses procedural drawing and requires no image assets or external plugin installation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Macro Knob\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A single macro control for REAPER parameter links. It uses the same charcoal and amber interface as ReaCrusher, with scaled typography, vertical dragging, Shift for fine changes, wheel adjustment, and double-click or right-click reset. Audio and MIDI pass through unchanged.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 XY Pad\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A four-source stereo blender: route four stereo sources to channels 1\u8211-8 and blend them with the pad. It retains equal-power interpolation, smooth XY movement, and the linked output limiter. The panel uses ReaCrusher's palette and typography, with matching ceiling/release knobs, source-weight indicators and a gain-reduction readout. Shift-drag for fine movement; double-click the pad to centre it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install with ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Import this repository URL in {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Import repositories}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mannixsquared/JSFX/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Browse packages, search for ReaCrusher, Macro Knob, or XY Pad, and install the effects you want. Then refresh REAPER's FX browser. The adjacent {\f1 .rpl} bank is imported on first use. If the effect was previously installed, use {\b + \u8594 ? Import preset library (.rpl)} in its native preset toolbar.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Manual installation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copy the {\f1 .jsfx} files you want from {\f1 Effects/} into your REAPER resource folder's {\f1 Effects} directory. For ReaCrusher, copy its {\f1 .rpl} file alongside it. Open the FX browser and search for the effect name.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Drag vertically to adjust; Shift-drag for fine changes, scroll to adjust, and double-click to reset a knob. See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "USER_GUIDE.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
USER_GUIDE.md
}}}
 for DSP details.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 License\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copyright (C) 2026 Mannix Squared. Licensed under GNU GPL version 3 or later; see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "LICENSE"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
LICENSE
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Development and updates\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The {\f1 main} branch is indexed by GitHub Actions. Increase {\f1 @version} in {\f1 Effects/ReaCrusher.jsfx}, update {\f1 @changelog}, then push to publish an update. Keep the effect's filename and category path stable to preserve project references. The generated {\f1 index.xml} points to committed file versions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Adding effects\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Add each effect as a separate {\f1 .jsfx} package under a category directory such as {\f1 Effects/}. Give each package its own version and metadata header, and list any companion files with {\f1 @provides}. Mark shared scripts and development helpers {\f1 @noindex}. All packages share this repository\u8217's ReaPack index.\par}
}
